WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.800
From the Tibetan Plateau, the Yellow River flows
over 5,000 kilometers to the sea.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.800
Crossing the Loess Plateau, it picks up
enormous amounts of sediment.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.800
Chinese civilization grew along its banks.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.800
Floods long threatened its banks,
and the lower reach once ran dry.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.800
Today, dams, laws and careful water and sediment
management keep it flowing.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.800
The Yellow River, often called the mother river
of China, flows on.